From a5cb0f47c415672f5a7ccb8bbe70b37948645904 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raimondas Lencevicius <59739769+raimondasl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:16:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] Add payload snapshot tests for the rolling-summary
 profiles

Extends the Gemini 3.8 Flash high payload snapshots to the two
rolling-summary profiles and replaces the notes-off stand-in (the Standard
profile with the flag off) with the checked-in
google-gemini-3-8-flash-high-rolling-summary-notes-off.

- rolling-summary and notes-off: the full request bodies through a 175k
  trigger. Before it, only visible user/model text; at it, one summary
  request (SUMMARY_SYSTEM_PROMPT, the whole text history, 8,192-token
  cap); after it, the user-role bridge followed by the new observation.
  No request carries thought steps, signatures or reasoning summaries.
- Notes-off equals the Provider Adapter request for request, including the
  summary request, once the Adapter's thought steps and SDK annotations
  are removed: the last path step adds only native replay.
- The same holds when a lost life buffers a GAME_OVER frame just before
  the summary: both profiles summarize that unpresented frame and restart
  from the bridge (the Google adapter at this commit does not implement
  the later PendingCompactionInputs protocol).
- Rolling-summary equals notes-off except the carry-forward sentence.
- Drop-oldest never fires: with ~12k-character observations and one
  provider token per character, Standard drops turns above 175k
  characters while rolling-summary compacts instead; every action request
  starts with the first observation or a bridge, and run_meta records
  context_trims=0.
- The cross-profile checks (notes sentence, thinking_level=high,
  service_tier on every request, config validation) now cover all four
  profiles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
